# This Function imports `sanity-plugin-i18n/core`, the plugin's framework-free entry
# point, which has no runtime dependency on React, `sanity` or `@sanity/ui`.
#
# The plugin still declares those as peerDependencies, because its *other* entry point
# is a Studio plugin and that constraint is what stops it being installed into an
# incompatible Studio. npm auto-installs peer dependencies, though, so without this file
# `npm install` here drags the entire Sanity Studio into a Node function that never
# touches it: 981 packages and 564 MB, versus 59 packages and 42 MB with it.
#
# This lives in .npmrc rather than in the documented install command on purpose: it then
# applies to any `npm install` run in this folder, including the one Sanity's remote
# Function builder runs, which we do not control.
omit=peer
